        "original_id": "ffbe9434-313d-56dc-b795-9c19914c208f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Allison J71, Allison J35\n- Concepts: single-spool turbojet engines, afterburners, thrust\n- Places: United States\n\nFacts:\n- In 1948, development of the Allison J71 began as a heavily modified Allison J35 and it was originally designated J35-A-23.\n- The Allison J71 was a single-spool turbojet engine designed and built in the United States.\n- Most Allison J35 models carried an afterburner.\n- With the afterburner, the Allison J35 produced 7,400 lbf of thrust.",
